 "notes": "Outputs: the ground truth's four ARN outputs each carry a Condition that is false under defaults, so its normalised view has none and an output check would fail on it; 'every subscription exposes its ARN as an output' stays unchecked (tested against the fixture). The sentinel comparison lives in Conditions, which aren't in the normalised input, so subs_conditional shows each subscription is gated, not what gates it. endpoints_from_parameters requires each endpoint's value to equal a parameter default, which also shows the parameter has a sentinel default. PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt calls the topic ARN 'required' but the ground truth gives SNSTopicArn a placeholder default; no check on required-ness, and a parameter with or without a default both pass topic_arn_from_input. endpoints_not_provisioned is detail while topic_not_provisioned is core because the topic is the scenario's primary input and the endpoints are a trailing clause. Nearly every requirement here is primary, so the core share is high on purpose."
